{
    "background_story": "Makai was a quiet, introspective boy who found solace in the classic board game Parcheesi. Growing up in a large, boisterous family, he often felt lost in the chaos. But whenever he sat down to play Parcheesi with his grandmother, he felt a sense of calm wash over him. She taught him the intricacies of the game, and he quickly became a master strategist. As he entered adulthood, Makai's love for Parcheesi never faded. He began competing in local tournaments, where his focused nature and analytical mind served him well. Before long, he became a regional champion, earning the nickname 'The Parcheesi Prodigy.' Makai's success in the game brought him out of his shell, and he formed lasting bonds with fellow players who shared his passion.",
